---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout title="Home" fullBleed>
  <div class="hero">
    <video class="hero-video" autoplay muted loop playsinline>
      <source src={`${base}videos/backgrounds/home.mp4`} type="video/mp4" />
    </video>
    <img src={`${base}logo_tourney_balance.png`} alt="Tourney Balance" class="hero-logo" />
  </div>

  <div class="page-body">
    <div class="page-body-inner">
      <h1>Welcome to Tourney Balance</h1>
      
      <p>
        <strong>This site catalogues the balance changes and patch history of the mod.</strong>
      </p>

      <p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href={`${base}changes/`}>Read the Balance Changes →</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${base}patch-notes/`}>Read the most recent Patch Notes →</a></li>
      </ul>
      </p>

      <h2>What is Tourney Balance</h2>
      <p>
        Tourney Balance is a balance mod for high difficulty modded gameplay of Warhammer: Vermintide 2.

        It aims to rebalance many classes and weapons by nerfing overperformers and 
        buffing weaker or lesser used options, improving variety and choice for players.
        
        Despite numerous adjustments to numbers and values, the goal is to stay as close to the 
        feel of official game balance as possible, so that play styles and the original design 
        intent are retained.
      </p>
      <p>
        Tourney Balance mostly focuses on balancing around the Cataclysm 3 Deathwish Onslaught
        (C3DWONS) difficulty and its higher difficulty versions, such as C3DWONS+ and C3DWUTCH. 
        The original intention of Tourney Balance is to serve as the baseline for the various tourneys 
        held in the modded scene, such as the Onslaught Series.
      </p>

      <h2>Features</h2>
      <p>
        Alongside its balance changes, the mod also includes several tools
        used for events and basic quality-of-life improvements:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Mod Checker</strong> — displays any banned tournament mods currently used by you or your team.</li>
        <li><strong>Disable Bots</strong> — disables bots and removes their portraits.</li>
        <li><strong>Pause</strong> — pauses the game.</li>
        <li><strong>Restart</strong> — restarts the current game.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Community</h2>
      <p>
        If you would also like to join the modded scene — be it for tourneys, regular games, or just discussions about the mods in
        question — feel free to join the <a href="https://discord.gg/MS4vWSQrEh">Onslaught Series</a> and <a href="https://discord.gg/hyeADkwp">VT Modded Community</a> Discord servers!
      </p>
      <p>
        The source code for the mod can be found <a href="https://github.com/Camilo-Guzman/Tourney-Balance">here</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Credits</h2>
      <p>
        Thanks to the Tourney Balance Team, and the continued support and feedback from many different community members, 
        the mod is still receiving updates.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero {
    position: relative;
    height: 30vh;
  }

  .hero-video {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 100vw;
    height: 100vh;
    object-fit: cover;
    z-index: -1;
  }

  .hero-logo {
    position: absolute;
    top: 3rem;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    max-width: min(50vw, 480px);
    height: auto;
  }

  .page-body {
    position: relative;
    background: linear-gradient(
      to bottom,
      rgba(18, 18, 18, 0) 0%,
      rgba(18, 18, 18, 1) 3%,
      rgba(18, 18, 18, 1) 67%,
      rgba(18, 18, 18, 0.7) 100%
    );
    width: 100vw;
    margin-left: calc(50% - 50vw);
    margin-right: calc(50% - 50vw);
  }

  .page-body-inner {
    max-width: 1100px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem;
  }
</style>
